 },
 "summary": "A red warning with red LAND ASAP. Smoke is detected in the aft cargo hold, which is built to contain a fire, so the smoke is not felt in the cockpit; only the SMOKE light on the CARGO SMOKE panel confirms it. Close the aft isolation valve if it did not close by itself, cabin fans OFF, discharge AGENT 1 (guarded pb, crosscheck first) and AGENT 2 after 60 min, and divert. Expect the warning to stay after discharge. On the ground, the passengers disembark before any cargo door is opened.",
