 "background": [
  {
   "text": "The cargo compartments are designed to be air-tight and fireproof to contain a fire, and the cargo ventilation prevents cargo smoke from reaching the cockpit/cabin. The crew can only confirm the alert with the SMOKE light on the CARGO SMOKE panel.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 9/10",
     "pdf": 506
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The aft compartment has four smoke detectors on two loops. The warning needs both detectors of a cavity (or one, if the other is inoperative). The isolation valves close and the extraction fan stops automatically.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-26-50-10",
     "page": "P 3/8",
     "pdf": 1546
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The DISCH pb fires the squibs of the fire bottles: bottle 1 discharges in about 60 s; a flow metering system controls bottle 2 for at least 135 min. BTL 1(2) light amber when empty.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-26-50-10",
     "page": "P 5/8",
     "pdf": 1548
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The DISCH sw is guarded. The DISCH AGENT 2 light comes on amber 60 min after AGENT 1 and goes off when the AGENT 2 squib is ignited.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCOM",
     "code": "DSC-26-50-20",
     "page": "P 3/4",
     "pdf": 1554
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "technique": [
  {
   "text": "An immediate diversion should be considered as soon as smoke/fumes are detected. If the source is not immediately obvious, accessible and extinguishable, divert without delay.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 1/10",
     "pdf": 498
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Guarded controls are crosschecked by both pilots before acting in flight.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "AOP-30-20",
     "page": "P 1/2",
     "pdf": 80
    },
    {
     "book": "PDP",
     "code": "Management of abnormal operations",
     "page": "XFTDN6ECAM00001",
     "pdf": 432
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "If smoke/fumes become perceptible in the cockpit or cabin, or any doubt exists about the smoke origin, apply the [QRH] SMOKE / FUMES / AVNCS SMOKE procedure.",
   "applies_to": [
    "all"
   ],
   "refs": [
    {
     "book": "FCTM",
     "code": "PR-AEP-SMOKE",
     "page": "P 1/10",
     "pdf": 498
    },
    {
     "book": "PDP",
     "code": "Smoke",
     "page": "XFTDA1SMOKE0001",
     "pdf": 535
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
